---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
import LangSwitch from '../../../components/LangSwitch.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of use of the Nino Rush app | Ludiven Studio"
	description="Terms of use and sale of the Nino Rush mobile game: free demo, the full adventure as an in-app purchase, optional account, coins and looks, purchases, videos of our games, level workshop, liability, governing law."
	lang="en"
	alternates={{ fr: '/nino-rush/cgu/', en: '/en/nino-rush/cgu/', es: '/es/nino-rush/cgu/', de: '/de/nino-rush/cgu/', it: '/it/nino-rush/cgu/' }}
>
	<div class="wrapper stack gap-12 legal">
		<div class="stack gap-8">
			<LangSwitch
				lang="en"
				links={[
					{ lang: 'fr', href: '/nino-rush/cgu/' },
					{ lang: 'es', href: '/es/nino-rush/cgu/' },
					{ lang: 'de', href: '/de/nino-rush/cgu/' },
					{ lang: 'it', href: '/it/nino-rush/cgu/' },
				]}
			/>
			<Hero
				title="Terms of use — Nino Rush"
				tagline="A free demo, then the whole adventure in one purchase."
			/>
		</div>

		<p class="updated">
			<strong>Nino Rush</strong> app (<code>com.ludivenstudio.ninorush</code>) — last updated: November 6,
			2026.
		</p>
		<p class="updated">
			This is a courtesy translation. In case of discrepancy, the
			<a href="/nino-rush/cgu/" hreflang="fr">original French version</a> prevails.
		</p>

		<div class="summary">
			<p><strong>Key points before you play:</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li>The game is a <strong>free</strong> download, with a demo: the start of the adventure, the whole level workshop and the first puzzles. It plays with no account and no network.</li>
				<li><strong>The full adventure</strong>, a one-time purchase, opens every other world and every puzzle. The big wardrobe, optional, opens every look sold for coins. No subscription.</li>
				<li>Purchases, behind a question for grown-ups, go through <strong>Google Play or the App Store</strong>. They <strong>never change the rules of a level</strong>, nor how Nino rolls.</li>
				<li>Coins and looks <strong>have no cash value</strong>: they cannot be traded, resold or refunded, except where the law requires it.</li>
				<li>The game is for ages <strong>13 and up</strong>. Workshop levels are shared through codes you paste yourself: <strong>no online levels, no chat</strong>.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>1. Purpose and acceptance</h2>
			<p>
				These terms govern the use of the Nino Rush mobile game (hereinafter "the Game") and the sale of its
				paid content. By installing or using the Game, you accept them. If you refuse them, do not use the Game
				and uninstall it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>2. Publisher</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Company name: <strong>Ludiven Studio</strong></li>
				<li>Legal form: EURL (French single-member limited company) with share capital of €1,000</li>
				<li>Registration: 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586 R.C.S. Vienne — SIRET 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586&nbsp;00013</li>
				<li>EU VAT number: FR20&nbsp;999253586</li>
				<li>Registered office: 1166 route de la Ranche, 38440 Châtonnay, France</li>
				<li>Publication director: Ludiven Studio</li>
				<li>Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a></li>
			</ul>
			<p>See also the <a href="/mentions-legales/">legal notice</a> (in French).</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>3. The Game</h2>
			<p>
				Nino Rush is a platform game: you roll Nino, a red panda, from world to world all the way to his burrow.
				It also offers boulder chases, crate smashes, puzzles, a workshop to make your own levels, a sticker
				album and looks for Nino.
			</p>
			<p>
				The Game is a free download, with a <strong>demo</strong>: the first worlds, with their boulder chases and
				crate smashes, the whole workshop and the first puzzles. <strong>The full adventure</strong>, sold in the
				Game (see §6), opens every other world and every puzzle.
			</p>
			<p>
				Playing needs no account and no network. Videos, purchases and the online copy of your progress need
				the internet. Connection and equipment costs are borne by you.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>4. Account (optional)</h2>
			<p>
				The Game is played <strong>without an account</strong>: your progress is then kept on your phone only,
				and you may lose it if you uninstall the Game or change phones. To keep a copy online and get it back on
				another phone, you can sign in with your <strong>Google</strong> account, or <strong>Apple</strong> on
				iPhone, in Settings › "Account". This account is the <strong>Ludiven Studio account</strong>, which is
				also used by the studio's other games, the Pétanque Meet app and the website.
			</p>
			<p>
				The Game is for ages <strong>13 and up</strong>. If you are a minor, ask your parents before a purchase;
				if you are under 15, also before signing in.
			</p>
			<p>
				You are responsible for what is done from your account. Keep access to your Google or Apple account: it
				is what lets you get your online progress back. An account cannot be transferred or sold.
			</p>
			<p>
				You can delete your account at any time: Settings › "Account" › "Delete account". Deletion is final and
				also applies to the studio's other games, Pétanque Meet and the website: the online copy of your
				progress cannot be given back. The progress on your phone stays. What is erased is described in the
				<a href="/en/nino-rush/confidentialite/#suppression">privacy policy</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>5. Coins and looks</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>Coins</strong> are collected by playing; at the end of a level, an optional video of one of our
				other games can double those of the level (see §8). They are used to buy <strong>looks</strong> for Nino:
				colors, hats and trails. The big wardrobe (see §6) opens every look sold for coins at once. Some looks
				can only be earned with crowns or stickers.
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Coins and looks are a <strong>personal user license</strong> within the Game. You do not own them.</li>
				<li>They <strong>have no cash value</strong>: they cannot be converted into money, traded between players, resold or refunded, except where the law requires it.</li>
				<li>Looks only change how Nino looks, never how he rolls: <strong>no purchase changes a rule or a goal</strong>.</li>
				<li>Without an account, they are only on your phone and may disappear if you uninstall the Game. Signed in, they are also kept online until you delete your account.</li>
				<li>The publisher may change the coin prices and the catalog of looks. A look you already have stays yours. Coins or looks obtained through an error in the Game, through cheating or through a refunded purchase may be taken away.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>6. Purchases</h2>
			<p>The Game sells, for real money, in its shop, behind a question for grown-ups:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>the full adventure</strong>: every world after the demo and every puzzle;</li>
				<li>the <strong>big wardrobe</strong>, optional: every look that can be bought with coins, all at once; these looks can also be earned by playing.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				These are two one-time, permanent purchases, with no subscription. The price is the one shown in the Game
				at the time of purchase, in your currency, including taxes. A price change has no effect on purchases
				already made.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Payment goes exclusively through Google Play or the App Store</strong>, depending on your
				phone, and follows their terms. The publisher has no access to any banking data. The proof of purchase
				is issued by the store. On top of the Game's question, parental controls on purchases are those of the
				store.
			</p>
			<p>
				The full adventure and the big wardrobe are tied to your Google Play or App Store account: after a
				reinstall, or on another phone linked to the same account, "Restore purchases", in the shop, gives them
				back. If you are signed in to your Ludiven Studio account, your online progress keeps them too. If a
				purchase is not credited, write to us with the store's proof of purchase.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>7. Right of withdrawal and refunds</h2>
			<p>
				The full adventure and the big wardrobe are digital content supplied immediately after purchase. In
				accordance with Article L221-28 13° of the French Consumer Code, by requesting their immediate supply,
				you <strong>waive your right of withdrawal</strong> of fourteen days, which you acknowledge at the time
				of purchase.
			</p>
			<p>
				Refunds are handled by the store where the purchase was made, under its rules:
				<a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT204084" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple</a> or
				<a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Play</a>.
				We cannot refund in their place, but we can help you with the process: write to us. Your statutory
				guarantees of conformity remain in force.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>8. Videos of our games</h2>
			<p>
				At the end of a level, the Game offers a short video of one of our other games or apps, which doubles
				your coins, always by your choice and five times a day at most. The Game shows no advertising from
				other companies. What the Game reads on our website for these videos is described in the
				<a href="/en/nino-rush/confidentialite/">privacy policy</a> (§3).
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>9. The workshop and level codes</h2>
			<p>
				The workshop lets you make your own levels; they stay on your phone. "Share" copies a level's code to
				the clipboard: you choose where to paste it and whom to send it to. A code holds the level, a name drawn
				at random from word lists and your best time: no free text, nothing about you.
			</p>
			<p>
				The Game hosts no level: there are <strong>no online levels, no chat and no messages</strong>. A code
				from another player is added with "Paste a code"; the Game refuses a code it cannot read. Workshop levels
				earn nothing and do not count in your progress.
			</p>
			<p>
				Codes are exchanged outside the Game, under the responsibility of those who share them: the publisher
				does not see them and is not liable for where they are posted.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>10. Intellectual property</h2>
			<p>
				The Game, its code, its images, its animations, its sounds, its music, its texts and its characters,
				including Nino, belong to Ludiven Studio or its licensors and are protected by intellectual property
				law. You receive a personal, non-exclusive right of use. Components by other authors remain their
				authors', under their licenses, listed in the Game (Settings › "Credits").
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>11. Changes, interruption and discontinuation of the service</h2>
			<p>
				The publisher may change the Game, add or remove features, and adjust the coin prices and the winnings.
				The online copy of your progress and the videos rely on our providers: they may be interrupted for
				maintenance or by an outage.
			</p>
			<p>
				The publisher may stop all or part of the service, in particular if running it is no longer viable or
				if a store requires its removal. It will then tell players, with reasonable notice. Levels will remain
				playable as long as the installed version works on your phone. Discontinuation does not give rise to a
				refund of the full adventure or of the big wardrobe, except where the law requires it.
			</p>
			<p>
				These terms may change. The date of the update appears at the top of the page. In the event of a
				significant change, we will let you know; continuing to play means you accept them.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>12. Liability</h2>
			<p>
				The Game is provided as is. The publisher does not guarantee that it works without interruption or
				error on all phones, nor that the online services are always available.
			</p>
			<p>
				The publisher can only be held liable in the event of proven fault, and its liability is limited to
				direct and foreseeable damage. It does not cover progress kept only on the phone and lost, nor progress
				lost through the deletion of the account or the loss of access to the Google or Apple account, nor level
				codes exchanged outside the Game. Nothing here excludes its liability in the event of gross negligence
				or physical injury, nor limits your mandatory consumer rights.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>13. Personal data</h2>
			<p>
				The processing of your data is described in the
				<a href="/en/nino-rush/confidentialite/">Nino Rush privacy policy</a>, which forms part of these terms.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>14. Governing law and disputes</h2>
			<p>
				These terms are governed by <strong>French law</strong>. If you are a consumer living in another member
				state of the European Union, you keep the mandatory protections of your country.
			</p>
			{/* TODO legal: replace with the mediator's name, address and website once adhesion is signed (art. L612-1). */}
			<p>
				If there is a problem, write to us first: we will look for an amicable solution. If there is no
				solution within one month, you can turn to a consumer mediator free of charge (Article L612-1 of the
				French Consumer Code). The mediator's contact details are given on request at
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>. Failing agreement, the
				dispute will be brought before the competent courts.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>15. Contact</h2>
			<p>
				For any question or to report a problem:
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.legal {
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
		color: var(--gray-200);
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}
	.legal ul {
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.35rem;
	}
	.legal a {
		color: var(--accent-regular);
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}
	.legal a:hover,
	.legal a:focus {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}
	.updated {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-300);
	}
	.summary {
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-regular);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
	}
	.summary p {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	code {
		font-size: 0.9em;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
		padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
		border-radius: 0.25em;
	}
</style>
